Atelier's architecture is grounded in our organization's own validated documents, including care protocols, HAS recommendations, internal procedures, regulatory texts, and internal guides. This ensures that our solution provides explainable recommendations or suggestions, with every answer generated by our system citing the retrieved passages used to create it. Our approach involves corpus selection and curation, retrieval tuning, prompt and template design, and an evaluation loop to ensure the quality of the solution.

Our platform operates 24/7 with an active-active setup across two availability zones, ensuring high availability and meeting the requirement for around-the-clock service. Atelier provides API-first design (REST + webhook) with documented APIs that can be embedded in existing work environments, allowing seamless integration with the hospital information system and electronic patient record.

To address data sovereignty concerns, we offer hosting options on OuraneCloud's Sovereign HDS tier, which is SecNumCloud-qualified, HDS-certified, and located within the EU. This setup ensures that all data processing and storage are performed within the EU, adhering to strict data sovereignty and privacy regulations.

Our solution complies with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and French health data hosting (HDS) certification requirements. We guarantee strict compliance with GDPR Article 9 for special-category health data and ensure medical confidentiality (secret médical) is preserved. Our data protection measures include encryption in transit using TLS 1.3, encryption at rest using AES-256, key management through EU-based infrastructure, pseudonymisation, data minimization, and configurable retention.

The proposed solution integrates with the existing hospital information system (SIH) and electronic patient record (DPI), supporting health interoperability standards (HL7/FHIR) and the national health identifier (INS). Our platform is aligned with the Ségur du numérique en santé framework and supports Mon espace santé/DMP, ensuring compliance with France's national healthcare digitization strategy.

To optimize costs and enhance our margin, we propose a phased implementation approach. This involves starting with a pilot phase in one or two departments, followed by progressive generalization to all services. Our standard daily rates range from €700 for an engineer to €1,300 for a project director. The cost of hosting and inference varies materially with the chosen tier and model but is a main recurring cost driver.

Our target gross margin percentage ranges from 25% to 35%. Assuming we can maintain our standard daily rates and considering the mix of services required by the client, our cost structure for one-off project costs such as framing, design, integration, change management, and training, as well as recurring run costs like platform subscription, hosting/infrastructure, model-inference costs, support, and maintenance, will be a significant portion of the budget.

The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at €900,000 over 5 years. Our approach ensures that annual operating costs remain controlled and compatible with the authority's budgetary capacity. By leveraging our Sovereign HDS Tier and Sovereign European Model, we can reduce recurring costs while maintaining high-quality service delivery.

In terms of innovation strategy, we propose a progressive deployment, starting with a pilot phase in one or two departments, followed by gradual generalization to all services. This approach allows us to test and refine the solution while minimizing disruption to clinical and administrative workflows. Our model options include a sovereign European open-weight model (self-hosted) that provides strong grounding behavior and is well-suited to explainability-driven and sovereignty-driven requirements.

To reduce the environmental footprint of our solution, we partner with OuraneCloud, which offers sovereign hosting in the EU, renewable energy, and a low power usage effectiveness (PUE) of 1.2. Our approach contributes to reducing energy consumption and relies on low-carbon infrastructure, aligning with the client's goal of limiting the environmental impact of their information systems.

Our project management team will work closely with the client to ensure a smooth deployment process. We propose a hybrid delivery model that combines agile iterations with a phase-gate structure, suited for public and health procurement projects like this one. Our two-week sprints with demonstrable increments will allow us to adapt quickly to any changes or feedback from the client during the pilot phase.

In conclusion, our consortium proposes a comprehensive AI-powered platform, Atelier, designed to meet the CHRB's requirements for an AI assistance solution. Our approach ensures high availability, seamless integration, and compliance with regulatory requirements while minimizing environmental impact. We are confident that our solution will improve the efficiency of CHRB's staff and enhance the quality and safety of patient care.
